This repository combines two things with different provenance.

1. THE PROJECT SCAFFOLDING
   The PreTeXt project structure, build configuration, and workflow files
   originate from Oscar Levin's PreTeXt course template and remain under
   the MIT License reproduced below.

2. THE COURSE CONTENT
   The prose, section introductions, and the selection and arrangement of
   exercises under source/ are Copyright (c) 2026 Kyle Ormsby and
   contributors, Reed College.

   TODO: choose a license for the content. A Creative Commons license
   (CC BY-SA 4.0 or CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) is the usual choice for open
   textbooks, and Runestone Academy requires an open license -- either
   GNU-FDL or Creative Commons -- if the book is ever hosted there.
   Worth confirming with Reed before announcing this publicly.

   The WeBWorK problems themselves are not part of this repository. They
   are referenced by path into the Open Problem Library and carry their
   own licenses from their original authors.

